      "value": "@{5a69eccdd20e79665351e7c1|full_name}: I've had them for a couple of weeks and, while not perfect, it's not that bad? They can fail sometimes, but moving/drumming your fingers a bit fixes it (at least in my case). You don't even have to keep the gesture: you can enable gestures, do it to activate whatever animation you assigned to it, then disable the gestures so it gets stuck and pose your hand however you want.",
