      "value": "@{5a95256f54d514123c1f089d|full_name}: The thing is Oculus controllers work perfectly, so coming from an Oculus it feels absolutely awful when you can't rely on your hands. I imagine this is what it's like to have nerve damage or a brain tumor IRL. Just randomly can't use your body right. It sucks compared to the Oculus controls. Individual finger movement wasn't worth this, but sadly getting the Oculus controllers working with an Index headset isn't possible, so we just have to deal with Valve's mishap.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
